DESCRIPTION >
    Phase 4a (Pattern B row-pull). Flat, site-scoped, lookback-windowed pull of
    `$pageview` rows — NOT filtered per-visitor (matches today's behavior exactly).
    Replaces the HogQL `pvSql` in `getMultiTouchAttributionLive`
    (api/lib/attribution-engine.js:1478), shared by linear/u_shaped/time_decay/
    w_shaped — see tinybird/PHASE4_BUILD_PLAN.md §0 for why these 4 models share
    one pipe pair, and tinybird/PHASE4_4A_FIELD_MAPPING.md §2/§4 for the verified
    column mapping and the window-pin requirement (guardrail 4).
    Caller MUST compute `lookback_from` using the exact ternary at
    api/lib/attribution-engine.js:1464-1467 (reusing serializeHogQLDateTime/
    serializeHogQLDateRange) — do not reimplement the windowDays/'ltv' logic here.
    `custom_key1`/`custom_key2` are optional — mirrors the dynamic
    custom_param:<key> SELECT at api/lib/attribution-engine.js:1469-1476 (only the
    1-2 keys the active groupBy/groupBy2 request actually needs).
    NOT YET VALIDATED against the live schema (no `tb build`/`tb push` run —
    pending founder go-ahead on cloud-touching CLI commands, see Phase 4a report).

TOKEN "phase4_pageviews_read" READ

NODE pageviews_windowed_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        distinct_id,
        timestamp,
        utm_source,
        utm_medium,
        utm_campaign,
        referrer,
        ai_source,
        gclid,
        gbraid,
        wbraid,
        fbclid,
        msclkid,
        ttclid,
        li_fat_id,
        li_fatid,
        twclid,
        dclid,
        snapclid,
        pclid,
        sccid,
        ko_click_id,
        page_url,
        utm_term
        {% if defined(custom_key1) %}, JSONExtractString(properties, {{ String(custom_key1) }}) AS custom_key1{% end %}
        {% if defined(custom_key2) %}, JSONExtractString(properties, {{ String(custom_key2) }}) AS custom_key2{% end %}
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$pageview'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(lookback_from, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
    ORDER BY timestamp ASC
    LIMIT 100000

TYPE endpoint
